{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785300636,"nonce":"r6R52fdkzcsyLDhB4Cf7M4WL50s=","message":"RCA:\n\nCode path: the patch-reply editor buffer is constructed entirely from\nthe locally applied commit, never from the original lore message.\n\n- src/b4/review_tui/_review_app.py:1268 (action_edit_reply): for a\n  patch (self._selected_idx \u003e 0) the buffer sources are\n  'git diff sha~1 sha' (line 1291-1294) for the quoted diff and\n  'git show --format=%B --no-patch sha' (line 1298-1300) for the\n  quoted message body.\n- Both are fed to _render_quoted_diff_with_comments()\n  (src/b4/review/_review.py:1816), which quotes commit_msg + diff.\n\nWhere the note is lost: content between the '---' cut line and the\ndiffstat exists only in the RFC822 message; 'git am' discards it on\napply, so the applied commit contains no trace of it. Since the reply\nbuffer is derived exclusively from that commit, the note can never\nappear in it.\n\nContrast: the follow-up reply path (_compose_followup_reply,\nsrc/b4/review_tui/_review_app.py:1692) quotes the stored email body of\nthe follow-up entry, so it does not have this problem — only the\npatch/cover reply path is commit-sourced.\n\nCause: reply construction deliberately anchors on the applied commit\n(the same real diff is used to re-anchor comment positions when the\nedited buffer is parsed back, _review_app.py:1283-1286), so the fix\nsurface touches the WYSIWYG buffer-is-source-of-truth design: the\nbelow-the-cut note would need to be sourced from the lore message\n(e.g. the cached thread blob) and merged into the quoted body.\n\nRelated bugs: none open on this path.","files":null}]}